  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1785777351988,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "id": "_UIlg299vYTMvdtwxvCLl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2114,
   "y": 1802,
   "width": 492.80000000000007,
   "height": 472.5,
   "text": "COVERAGE  (estimates - MEASURE BOTH ROWS IN WEEK 1)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n                       EuroPMC only   + full ladder\n raw OA full text        50-60%         70-75%\n METHODS-LEVEL FACTS     50-60%         80-88%   <- the target\n\nTHE REFRAME: you do not need the paper, you need the\nmethods facts. They live in 3 other places:\n\n 1 SR full text  = 10-20x leverage. One OA systematic\n   review carries characteristics-of-included-studies\n   (dose, form, population, n, duration) AND a RoB table\n   for ~15 primaries you cannot read.\n   -> FETCH SYNTHESES FIRST, THEN PRIMARIES.\n   -> inherited RoB penalty 0.85 (someone else's judgment,\n      gated by AMSTAR 2). No circularity: syntheses never\n      enter evidence mass anyway.\n\n 2 ct.gov RESULTS db is structured, not prose:\n   participant flow -> attrition (RoB 5), n, arms.\n\n 3 CONSORT structured abstracts carry randomisation,\n   blinding and n explicitly.\n\nNOT VIABLE: Elsevier/Wiley TDM (needs subscription),\nautomated institutional-login scraping (ToS violation,\nliability), pay-per-view (EUR 35-50/article).",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "mMIAKNV3-xTs-RuX4lpcO",
   "originalText": "COVERAGE  (estimates - MEASURE BOTH ROWS IN WEEK 1)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n                       EuroPMC only   + full ladder\n raw OA full text        50-60%         70-75%\n METHODS-LEVEL FACTS     50-60%         80-88%   <- the target\n\nTHE REFRAME: you do not need the paper, you need the\nmethods facts. They live in 3 other places:\n\n 1 SR full text  = 10-20x leverage. One OA systematic\n   review carries characteristics-of-included-studies\n   (dose, form, population, n, duration) AND a RoB table\n   for ~15 primaries you cannot read.\n   -> FETCH SYNTHESES FIRST, THEN PRIMARIES.\n   -> inherited RoB penalty 0.85 (someone else's judgment,\n      gated by AMSTAR 2). No circularity: syntheses never\n      enter evidence mass anyway.\n\n 2 ct.gov RESULTS db is structured, not prose:\n   participant flow -> attrition (RoB 5), n, arms.\n\n 3 CONSORT structured abstracts carry randomisation,\n   blinding and n explicitly.\n\nNOT VIABLE: Elsevier/Wiley TDM (needs subscription),\nautomated institutional-login scraping (ToS violation,\nliability), pay-per-view (EUR 35-50/article).",
   "autoResize": false,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "seed": 1941929779,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 25623236,
   "index": "b0176"
  },
