   "x": 2114,
   "y": 2792,
   "width": 462.00000000000006,
   "height": 840.0,
   "text": "STACK INVENTORY\n==========================================\nDATA APIs  (all free)\n Europe PMC REST      search + OA full text (JATS XML)\n PubMed E-utilities   MeSH, publicationType\n ClinicalTrials.gov   registry + RESULTS db (structured)\n Epistemonikos        SR -> included primaries\n OpenAlex             refs + best_oa_location\n Unpaywall            green OA resolution\n CORE.ac.uk           repository aggregator\n Crossref             metadata + retraction status\n\nSTATIC LISTS  (download once, refresh quarterly)\n Scimago SJR          journal quartile Q1-Q4   FREE\n predatory list       hard filter\n EFSA claims register calibration tier 1\n\n >> DO NOT USE JCR IMPACT FACTOR. Clarivate, paywalled,\n    expensive, and weakly predictive. SJR quartile does\n    the same job for free.\n\nPROCESSING  (no AI)\n JATS XML parser      Europe PMC full text - PREFER THIS\n                      over PDF wherever available\n GROBID               PDF -> structured header + refs\n                      self-hosted, free, right tool for\n                      included-study lists from PDFs\n PyMuPDF              raw PDF text fallback\n httpx + token bucket per-domain rate limiting\n\nINFRA\n Postgres 16          ECU store (btree on the 5-tuple)\n pg-boss              job queue, same DB, no extra service\n object store         cached XML/PDF, keyed by content hash\n pgvector             ONLY if S6 needs semantic NN. not yet.\n\nMODELS\n tier A  cheap/high volume   classify, simple extract\n tier B  mid                 extraction + judgment\n tier C  strong/low volume   outcome mapping, adjudication\n\n No fine-tuning at v1. Structured outputs + few-shot\n drawn from the anchor set.\n PICK TIERS BY A/B ON THE 28 ANCHORS, NOT BY PRICE LIST.\n\nROUGH COST  ~200-700 model calls per ingredient\n (50-150 studies x 3-5 calls). Order EUR 0.50-3.00\n per ingredient. ESTIMATE - instrument it in week 1.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "DhlEhxQYnDbHeQE96zwGk",
   "originalText": "STACK INVENTORY\n==========================================\nDATA APIs  (all free)\n Europe PMC REST      search + OA full text (JATS XML)\n PubMed E-utilities   MeSH, publicationType\n ClinicalTrials.gov   registry + RESULTS db (structured)\n Epistemonikos        SR -> included primaries\n OpenAlex             refs + best_oa_location\n Unpaywall            green OA resolution\n CORE.ac.uk           repository aggregator\n Crossref             metadata + retraction status\n\nSTATIC LISTS  (download once, refresh quarterly)\n Scimago SJR          journal quartile Q1-Q4   FREE\n predatory list       hard filter\n EFSA claims register calibration tier 1\n\n >> DO NOT USE JCR IMPACT FACTOR. Clarivate, paywalled,\n    expensive, and weakly predictive. SJR quartile does\n    the same job for free.\n\nPROCESSING  (no AI)\n JATS XML parser      Europe PMC full text - PREFER THIS\n                      over PDF wherever available\n GROBID               PDF -> structured header + refs\n                      self-hosted, free, right tool for\n                      included-study lists from PDFs\n PyMuPDF              raw PDF text fallback\n httpx + token bucket per-domain rate limiting\n\nINFRA\n Postgres 16          ECU store (btree on the 5-tuple)\n pg-boss              job queue, same DB, no extra service\n object store         cached XML/PDF, keyed by content hash\n pgvector             ONLY if S6 needs semantic NN. not yet.\n\nMODELS\n tier A  cheap/high volume   classify, simple extract\n tier B  mid                 extraction + judgment\n tier C  strong/low volume   outcome mapping, adjudication\n\n No fine-tuning at v1. Structured outputs + few-shot\n drawn from the anchor set.\n PICK TIERS BY A/B ON THE 28 ANCHORS, NOT BY PRICE LIST.\n\nROUGH COST  ~200-700 model calls per ingredient\n (50-150 studies x 3-5 calls). Order EUR 0.50-3.00\n per ingredient. ESTIMATE - instrument it in week 1.",
